# Install and publish against npmjs.org only.
#
# Without this, installs follow whatever registry the machine is configured
# with. A lockfile then records that registry's hostnames in `resolved`, which
# both publishes internal infrastructure and breaks `npm ci` for anyone off
# that network. It also risks resolving a peer dependency to a different build
# than users get from npm.
#
# Project-level so it applies to `npm i`, `npm ci`, `npm publish`, and CI
# without depending on anyone's ~/.npmrc.
#
# Note: this does not clean an already-regenerated lockfile. npm reuses
# `resolved` entries when versions and integrity are unchanged, so delete the
# lockfile and `node_modules/.package-lock.json` and regenerate instead.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/